🌐 Networking Portfolio

Overview

This section documents my hands-on networking learning journey, practical
Cisco networking labs, network configuration exercises, troubleshooting
activities, and networking-related certifications and badges.

My practical work focuses on building a strong foundation in network
infrastructure, Cisco IOS configuration, switching, VLANs, IPv4/IPv6
addressing, wireless networking, connectivity testing, troubleshooting,
and secure network administration.

The labs are primarily documented using Cisco Packet Tracer, supported by
screenshots, configuration documentation, verification results, and
practical exercises.

🎯 Networking Objectives

Through these labs and learning activities, I have developed practical
knowledge in:

- Network fundamentals
- Network devices and infrastructure
- Physical and logical network topologies
- Cisco IOS navigation
- Initial device configuration
- Switch configuration
- Router configuration
- VLAN configuration
- VLAN port assignment
- Network connectivity
- IPv4 addressing
- IPv6 concepts
- MAC and IP address identification
- Wireless networking
- Network troubleshooting
- Secure remote administration using SSH
- Network verification and documentation

